  "text": "We are given:\n\n- A **cylindrical log** with:\n  - **Diameter** = 2 feet → so the radius is 1 foot\n  - **Height** = 6 feet\n\n- A **plane cuts the log** through its **center** and **both top and bottom faces**.\n\n- The cross-section in the plane is a **trapezoid** with **two right angles**.\n\nWe are to find:\n\n- **Dimensions of the trapezoid**\n- **Angle between the plane and the horizontal**\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Geometry\n\nSince the log is a **cylinder**, and the plane cuts it through its **center**, the cross-section will be a **trapezoid** (a quadrilateral with two parallel sides) formed by slicing the cylinder.\n\nThe key is that the **cross-section is a trapezoid with two right angles**, meaning:\n\n- One side is a **horizontal** segment (the base of the trapezoid).\n- The other side is a **vertical** segment (the height of the trapezoid).\n- The two right angles are at the ends of the horizontal and vertical sides.\n\nThis makes the trapezoid a **rectangle**, since a rectangle has two right angles and two pairs of parallel sides.\n\nSo, the trapezoid is a **rectangle**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Dimensions of the Trapezoid\n\nSince the trapezoid is a rectangle:\n\n- The **height** of the trapezoid is the **height of the log** = 6 feet\n- The **width** of the trapezoid is the **diameter** of the log = 2 feet\n\nSo:\n\n- **Width = 2 feet**\n- **Height = 6 feet**\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Angle Between the Plane and the Horizontal\n\nThis is the **angle of inclination** of the trapezoid to the horizontal.\n\nSince the trapezoid is a **rectangle**, the angle between the plane (of the log) and the horizontal is **90 degrees**, because the trapezoid lies on the plane.\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n- **Dimensions of the trapezoid**:  \n  - **Width = 2 feet**  \n  - **Height = 6 feet**\n\n- **Angle between the plane and the horizontal**:  \n  - **90 degrees**\n\n$$\n\\boxed{\\text{Dimensions: width = 2 feet, height = 6 feet; angle = 90 degrees}}\n$$",
